-- title:
--   Rational integral function separating two supersingular places, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of the level-$M'$ function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A, M') = \kappa_A(jq, jq_{M'})$ over the residue field $\kappa_A$ of $A$, whose members are exactly the places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace` for $q$ and $M'$; assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$M'$ field $\mathbb{Q}$-generated by the divisor expansions, is contained in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ along $A$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A, M')$, that is: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose intersection with the constants is $A$, together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the reduced function field with kernel the maximal ideal, reducing constants through $A \to \kappa_A$, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with orders, and with every nonzero element scalable into the integers with nonzero residue; assume moreover the surjectivity law $hR_0$: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-coefficients lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally let $s \neq s'$ be two elements of $W$. Then there exists a Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ lying in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ such that its coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that for every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the inequality $\mathrm{ord}_P(j) \ge 0$ implies $\mathrm{ord}_P(g) \ge 0$, and such that the $R_0$-residue $\bar g$ lies in the valuation subrings of both $s$ and $s'$ and has distinct values there: $\mathrm{evalAt}_s(\bar g) \neq \mathrm{evalAt}_{s'}(\bar g)$.
--
--   This is the separation statement used in the supersingular bookkeeping on the level-$M'$ modular curve: two distinct supersingular points of the reduction are distinguished by the value of a single rational modular function which is integral for the constant reduction and regular wherever $j$ is. It is the $q = 2$ instance of the separation lemma, and feeds the constructions of rigid and node charts, of normal models and of Drinfeld-ring descent at level $M'$ for $q = 2$.
